    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Robert Jr.** stands out as the premier start with a score of 76.18, heavily buoyed by a favorable matchup against Jake Bennett. The combination of an advantageous platoon split and a slow delivery from Bennett, which maximizes our stolen base potential, makes **Luis Robert Jr.** an essential piece of our lineup. Alongside him, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.93) and **Gunnar Henderson** (66.25) provide high-floor production. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** (63.85) both benefit significantly from a positive park factor and the same favorable, slow-delivery pitching matchup, keeping them firmly in the strong play category despite facing left-handed pitching. **Henry Bolte** also earns a high recommendation (64.99) thanks to his leadoff positioning against Kade Anderson, where his sprint speed will be a critical asset in pursuing the scarcest category in our 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Miguel Vargas** (52.56), who narrowly missed the cut. While his underlying xwOBA remains solid at 0.389, he could not overcome the depth of our middle infield and corner utility options, specifically falling behind the higher upside of **Tommy White** and **Liam Hicks** in their respective matchups. As we look across the board, the entire lineup remains subject to confirmation of the posted batting orders, as we have utilized assumed placements; any significant shift down the order for **Liam Hicks** or **Tommy White** could compress their output further. We are also monitoring the status of **Andy Pages**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active depth to maximize our daily efficiency scores and maintain our push in the Roto standings.",
